# 1. Introduction

This project demonstrates the design and implementation of a Enterprise-Network-Design-using-OSPF in Cisco Packet Tracer.
The network consists of a **Head Office** and a **Branch Office** connected through a WAN. Internal communication is established using **OSPF dynamic routing**, while Internet connectivity is provided through an **Edge Router** configured with **NAT/PAT**.

The implementation also includes:

- VLAN Segmentation
- IEEE 802.1Q Trunking
- Router-on-a-Stick Inter-VLAN Routing
- Centralized DHCP Server
- DHCP Relay (IP Helper Address)
- Static Default Routing
- Switch Management VLANs

This project simulates a real enterprise network by integrating routing, switching, addressing, and Internet access into a single topology.

